    "updated_at": "2022-05-27T00:43:57Z",
    "body": "FWIW, building manually with cargo 1.61.0 (on an Intel Ubuntu 20.04 LTS system) fails for slightly different, but seemingly related, reasons:\r\n\r\n```\r\nerror: failed to run custom build command for `starship v1.7.1`\r\n\r\nCaused by:\r\n  process didn't exit successfully: `/tmp/cargo-install2qSCtZ/release/build/starship-c14a5b3276c1bcd4/build-script-build` (exit status: 127)\r\n  --- stderr\r\n  /tmp/cargo-install2qSCtZ/release/build/starship-c14a5b3276c1bcd4/build-script-build: error while loading shared libraries: libgit2.so.1.4: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory\r\n```",
